; DERIVED FROM THE SPRITE ART, NOT LEFT AS THE PLACEHOLDER GRAYS (the Vauban's SP5 ruling, re-run
; here). Measured 2026-09-20 with the same shader-literal test palette_swap_func.gdshaderinc uses
; (pixel == (v,0,0)/(0,v,0)/(0,0,v)/(0,v,v) for v in palette_index_r.png's seven red values 51, 85,
; 119, 153, 187, 221, 255): mf_sluagh.png (80x80, 2,875 opaque pixels) has ZERO channel-encoded
; pixels, so this scheme is INERT on this sprite exactly like the Vauban's and the Primrose's - it
; cannot repaint the token at all.
; So base_0..2 hold the sprite's OWN most-common literal fill colors (a plain colour census,
; excluding the pure-black linework at 49px/0,0,0): a grey-violet (113,108,123 - 109px), the bright
; violet (141,109,195 - 72px) and a near-black violet-grey (53,48,63 - 57px), most-used first per
; the Iskander's own slot convention. When real channel-encoded art replaces this sprite, it
; inherits a default that already looks like what the art shows today, instead of grey.
[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_colorscheme"]
script = ExtResource("3_colorscheme")
base_0 = Color(0.44313726, 0.42352942, 0.48235294, 1)
base_1 = Color(0.5529412, 0.42745098, 0.7647059, 1)
base_2 = Color(0.20784314, 0.1882353, 0.24705882, 1)

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_statblock"]
script = ExtResource("2_statblock")
size = 1
structure = 4
stress = 4
health = 8
armor = 0
evasion = 10
edef = 10
speed = 4
heat = 4
save_target = 10
sensor_range = 10
tech_attack = 1
repairs = 4
